            "subject": "LU-21014 lod: keep EC raid sets on distinct OSTs in RR"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Ronnie Sahlberg",
          "email": "rsahlberg@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-10-20 04:00:32.000000000",
          "tz": 600
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Ronnie Sahlberg",
          "email": "rsahlberg@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-10-22 06:04:24.000000000",
          "tz": 600
        },
        "subject": "LU-xxxxx lod: add kunit test for lod_comp_prep_create",
        "message": "LU-xxxxx lod: add kunit test for lod_comp_prep_create\n\nExport lod_ost_alloc_rr(), lod_ost_alloc_qos(), lod_comp_prep_create(),\nlod_lu_ops and lod_thread_key so a kunit test module can drive component\nallocation directly, without a mounted filesystem or live OSD/OSP under\neach OST. Add KUNIT_STATIC_STUB_REDIRECT() on the two allocators and on\nlod_qos_declare_object_on() so tests can force a given allocator or\nreplace object declaration with a fake dt_object.\n\nAdd lustre/kunit/lod_comp_test.c, exercising lod_comp_prep_create() for\nRR and QoS, forcing one allocator via stub while the other returns\n-EAGAIN. Cover:\n\n- FLR cross-mirror OST avoidance, including overstriped mirrors,\n  mirrors with different PFL boundaries, more mirrors than there are\n  OSTs to keep apart, and failure domains spanning OSSs.\n- EC data/parity pairing and raid-set aware allocation, with and\n  without overstriping, including layouts that must reuse parity or\n  data OSTs. Mirrors the allocation cases from sanity-ec 2b, 2c, 11,\n  13, 27a, 35a, 35b and 75c.\n- Mixed PFL layouts combining plain and EC components.\n- OSTs that are down, full, read-only, not creating, degraded, or\n  without precreated objects, including QoS falling back to RR, and\n  EC -C layouts that exhaust the unique OSTs under the same\n  conditions.\n- RR spreading stripes evenly across OSTs on several OSSs, and RR\n  preferring OSSs not already used by other mirrors.\n\nKnown issues: with too few failure domains, lod fails EC and FLR\ncreates, or gives a mirror fewer stripes than requested. These are\nadded as skipped known-issue cases until the desired behavior is\ndecided.\n\nRun from sanity test_51k, loading kunit on the MDS with enable=1 and\nchecking the KTAP output.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5\nChange-Id: I038664652cc29eccf512cc7ffe1fdb271c4dabb4\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
